WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.069 --> 00:00:10.080
As of filming this video, about 250 thousand
of you watched my recent hour long sit down

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:13.849
with Colin Moriarity from YouTube Week.

00:00:13.849 --> 00:00:18.840
Colin is best known as a gaming journalist
and one of the founders and host of Kinda

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:20.710
Funny, a popular gaming talk show.

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:26.170
I actually didn't know much about Colin before
our YouTube Week chat beyond a couple interactions

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:27.580
we had on Twitter.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:31.839
My intention with the interview was actually
to get away from politics and focus on my

00:00:31.839 --> 00:00:36.480
long lost love of video games, but within
a minute I could tell how passionate Colin

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.350
was about current events and the political
world.

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:43.789
Sometimes an interview you expect one thing
from, but get something totally different

00:00:43.789 --> 00:00:47.809
is the best kind, and in Colin's interview,
this was absolutely the case.

00:00:47.809 --> 00:00:51.739
Right after the interview, I told Colin that
he could be a major conservative political

00:00:51.739 --> 00:00:53.870
star if he ever wanted to go that route.

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:58.760
A few days after our initial interview, Colin's
world went completely bonkers.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:09.540
Colin posted a rather benign joke on Twitter
(Show tweet) on International Women's Day.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:14.240
The tweet got thousands of retweets and favorites,
but of course also caused backlash by the

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.680
Bigoteers always looking to be outraged.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:23.030
By the way, the joke itself, as Colin said,
isn't the smartest of funniest thing ever,

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:27.820
it's actually a really simple line that every
sitcom from I Love Lucy to Married With Children

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:31.130
to Everybody Loves Raymond has been based
on.

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:35.500
Regardless of whether it was funny or not,
a firestorm of outrage began and within a

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:40.270
couple days Colin stepped down from Kinda
Funny, the company he co-owned and the show

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:42.860
he co-created with his friends.

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:48.259
Regardless of whether the joke was funny,
or sexist or just stupid...which are all subjective

00:01:48.259 --> 00:01:54.690
feelings, the point is that the out of control
firestorm was once again on the attack.

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:59.549
The online gaming media jumped all over Colin,
in one case claiming he had gone on a right

00:01:59.549 --> 00:02:02.880
wing talk show known as The Rubin Report to
discuss the tweet.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:07.560
Of course in reality, we had taped and aired
the show about a week before he posted the

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.070
tweet in the first place.

00:02:09.070 --> 00:02:14.150
The worst case of journalistic dishonesty
came not from a gaming site though, but from

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:17.500
a mainstream outlet, the International Business
Times.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:19.840
Let's look at this headline:

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:26.419
KINDA FUNNY'S COLIN MORIARTY RESIGNS AFTER
TARGETING WOMEN IN A RACIST JOKE; INSISTS

00:02:26.419 --> 00:02:29.320
IT'S HIS PERSONAL DECISION

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:33.130
To say this is beyond the pale doesn't even
begin to describe it.

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:39.350
This social justice warrior disease, combined
with a pinch of intersectionality and a sprinkling

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:47.480
of misguided outrage has a mainstream publication
accusing Colin of racism where there literally

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:51.130
was not word word of racism in the tweet.

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:55.940
Eventually I was able to track down an editor
of IB Times, who I passed to Colin and they

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:59.250
changed the headline about 24 hours later.

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:03.230
Too little, too late, though, and the damage
was done.

00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:06.169
Just imagine if that had been you for a moment.

00:03:06.169 --> 00:03:11.220
This is what I mean when I say this regressive
movement will come for all of us.

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:17.729
I suspect coming for private citizens for
wrongthink is next, just wait and see.

00:03:17.729 --> 00:03:22.120
After all of this nonsense, I did a second
interview with Colin, live streamed out to

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:25.590
you with no editing, to clean up the mess.

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:30.220
Colin respectfully and honestly told his side
of the story, without throwing his friends

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:32.329
and former co-workers under the bus.

00:03:32.329 --> 00:03:36.950
We also took a ton of questions from you,
and shared a really intimate moment of friendship

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:37.950
on camera.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:44.220
When the interview finished, I really felt
like we had done something relevant and important.

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:50.150
Together we stood up against the outrage machine,
against the misguided social justice movement

00:03:50.150 --> 00:03:55.970
and more importantly, we stood up for something...for
ourselves...and if we won't stand for ourselves

00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:58.690
then why would anyone else stand for us?

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:00.750
Now this is where this really gets good.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:05.810
Last week Colin launched his own Patreon to
fund his new show aptly titled Colin's Last

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:06.810
Stand.

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:12.630
As of taping this he has over 30,000 a month
in pledges.

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:16.079
I'm beyond thrilled for him as a creator but
more so as a friend.

00:04:16.079 --> 00:04:22.070
It was only 10 days ago when he didn't know
if his career was over.

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:23.950
And I've been in the same boat myself.

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:28.910
Not only did Colin launch an incredibly successful
Patreon, but he's also made some stellar appearances

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:33.270
on Glenn Beck's radio show and last week was
on Joe Rogan's podcast.

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:38.300
I mention all of this because I view this
whole instance as a massive win for the free

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:40.020
speech, anti regressive movement.

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:45.760
We can no longer give these hysterical people
an inch because they won't stop taking until

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:47.700
we've all silenced ourselves.

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:52.810
Obviously many of you see this and agree with
it, which is not only why our interviews did

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:57.240
incredibly well but also why so many of you
put your money where your mouth is and joined

00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:58.690
Colin on Patreon.

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:02.500
And by the way I should welcome our new Patrons
as well because we got a bump in the midst

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:04.400
of all this as well.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:08.020
This isn't about money though, it's about
taking back the narrative from people who

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:14.530
use buzzwords and outrage to silence the rest
of us who are trying to have meaningful conversation.

00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:18.961
Allies are popping up all over the place in
this space and it's only together than we

00:05:18.961 --> 00:05:22.700
can full fight back the bad ideas which have
led us here.

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:27.810
From Colin to Joe Rogan to Phil DeFranco and
many others I see a new alliance forming of

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:32.510
content creators who aren't political per
se, but who will no longer be held hostage

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:37.750
by the same outrage machine that is crushing
dissent, not through conversation but by public

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:38.810
shaming.

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:43.620
We must now destroy the politics of destruction
if we're going to move forward.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:48.250
I think we just got a major win and I look
forward to you joining us for many more.

